===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|{{acronym of|en|[[Q]][[B]][[1]]}}|o}}.
Derived from '''QB1''' ("[[cue]] [[bee]] [[one]]"), short for '''[[w:(15760) 1992 QB1|(15760) 1992 QB1]]''', the first such object discovered

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌkjuːbiːˈwʌnoʊ/}} (that is, "QB1-o")

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|astronomy}} Any [[Kuiper belt object]] whose orbit is not determined by resonance with Neptune (orbit ~ 40-50 [[AU]]).

====Usage notes====
Somewhat old-fashioned, being generally replaced with ''classical Kuiper belt object.''

